#
Application Containerization (Docker) Documentation 
#
This application relies entirely on a containerized architecture for both local development and live production environments. 
By packaging the React frontend and Node.js backend into isolated Docker containers, we eliminate "it works on my machine" bugs and guarantee identical deployment behavior across all servers.
#
 1. Container Architecture SetupThe codebase splits the application into two separate optimized container environments defined by the master docker-compose.yml blueprint at the root of the project:


                     ┌────────────────────────────────┐
                     │     Master Docker Compose      │
                     └───────────────┬────────────────┘
                                     │
         ┌───────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┐
         ▼                                                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│       Frontend Container        │             │        Backend Container        │
│       (frontend/Dockerfile)     │             │       (backend/Dockerfile)      │
├─────────────────────────────────┤             ├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ • Build Layer: Node 22-Alpine   │             │ • Base Layer: Node 22-Alpine    │
│ • Production Host: Nginx Web OS │             │ • Active Port: 3001             │
│ • Active Port: 3000             │             │ • Shared Vol: backend/logs/     │
└─────────────────────────────────┘             └─────────────────────────────────┘
